# Developer-only catalog reproduction tools; not runtime dependencies.
tools
# Local editor worktrees and scratch QGIS profiles; a worktree holds a second copy
# of the plugin, which QGIS would try to load as a plugin of its own.
.claude
# Local working notes, not plugin documentation.
HANDOFF_NEXT_AGENT.md
# Repository-only content, not part of the installed plugin.
# Written by tools/generate_reference_manual.py (itself already excluded) and
# published online; no shipped code path opens a local copy.
# Same convention as planx_geostats.
MPYY_REFERENCE_MANUAL.html
# Repository-only content, not part of the installed plugin.
#
# docs/ is the source of the published manual and landing page; no shipped code
# path opens anything inside it -- every Help link resolves to the online manual
# at geophilo.com/planx_mpyy_studio/. Same convention as planx_suitability_lab
# and zero2cartolab.
docs
# A second, byte-identical copy of the whole tarama tile set: 969 files, 13.61 MB,
# which roughly doubles the archive's tile weight (the live set under resources/ is
# 956 files, 13.40 MB). No call site reaches it -- both tile resolvers build their
# path under resources/: core/mpyy_styler.py (the tile directory) and
# core/mpyy_workspace.py:529 (the SLD TARAMA placeholder token), and no shipped XML
# or JSON names "patterns" anywhere. Kept path-prefixed on purpose: _should_skip
# also matches on the basename, so a bare `patterns` would reach further than meant.
resources/patterns
